msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1867
msgid "Track races may publish times to 0.01 s while road races use whole seconds. Converting a 3:45 marathon split into decimal minutes for pace math is useful; inventing hundredths the watch never measured is not. Preserve the precision you actually recorded."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1437
msgid "Trail races may advertise a “10K” (kilometres) while US training plans talk in miles. Convert the race distance once and rebuild paces in your preferred unit."
msgstr "As corridas em trilha podem anunciar “10K” (quilômetros), enquanto os planos de treinamento dos EUA falam em milhas. Converta a distância da corrida uma vez e reconstrua os ritmos na sua unidade preferida."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2327
msgid "Train timetables that cross borders print local times per station. Differences require zone-aware subtraction; the resulting travel time is a duration you can convert to minutes for comparisons."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1417
msgid "Travel Distance: Kilometres and Miles"
msgstr "Distância de viagem: quilômetros e milhas"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2323
msgid "Travel examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2457
msgid "Treadmill buttons and silent unit switches"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2439
msgid "Treadmill Pace: min/km and Speed Units"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1253
msgid "Treat height as a length conversion problem with a clear target format. Decide whether the destination wants a single metric value (cm or m) or a dual customary pair (ft + in). Convert once, then format for display."
msgstr "Trate a altura como um problema de conversão de comprimento com um formato de destino claro. Decida se o destino deseja um valor métrico único (cm ou m) ou um par duplo habitual (ft + in). Converta uma vez e formate para exibição."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:322
msgid "Treating 1 oz as 25 g or 30 g shifts chocolate tempering and postage. “Net wt 16 oz” is one pound (453.6 g), not 16 × 30. Distinguish ounce-force if you came from an older engineering table."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:452
msgid "Treating 1.5 hours as 1 hour 50 minutes (decimal 0.5 ≠ 50). Flight “hours” in block time still convert with 60; time-zone offsets are a separate problem. Do not mix sexagesimal HMS strings without parsing each field."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:44
msgid "Treating 1/8″ as “3 mm” (true value ≈ 3.175 mm) stacks error across a part with many holes. Fractional inches must become decimals before multiplying. Do not confuse thousandths of an inch (mil) with millimetres—1 mil is 0.0254 mm, not 1 mm."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:180
msgid "Treating acres and hectares as equal roughly doubles or halves land area in conversation. Survey acres (especially older deeds) can differ slightly from the international acre—confirm the jurisdiction. Do not convert acre-feet (volume of irrigation water) with an area converter."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2041
msgid "Treating linear metres of skirting like square metres of carpet. Treating roll width as area. Forgetting hallways. Using interior paint-area estimates (which subtract windows) for flooring (which usually should not)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:230
msgid "Treating litres and m³ as interchangeable off-by-1000 errors. Rainfall in mm over an area yields litres or m³ only after multiplying by surface area—do not convert mm rain as if it were litres. Keep oil barrels and US gallons out of this SI-only path unless converted first."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:86
msgid "Treating metres and yards as equal is a ~9% error—enough to short a fabric order. Do not confuse square metres with square yards when buying sod or carpet; convert area separately. Survey “yards” in older deeds may not match the international yard."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2560
msgid "Trip computers may let you switch L/100 km ↔ mpg. After switching, reset averages; old samples mixed under another unit display still confuse humans even if the computer converted correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2532
msgid "Trip math before economy math"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1705
msgid "Trip time is distance divided by average speed—only when both use consistent length units. Mixing a 120 km leg with a 60 mph average without converting yields nonsense. Convert either all distances to miles and speeds to mph, or all to kilometres and km/h."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/default-suspense-and-error-boundary.tsx:117
msgid "Try again"
msgstr "Tentar novamente"

#: src/components/default-catch-boundary.tsx:34
msgid "Try Again"
msgstr "Tentar novamente"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1924
msgid "Two meanings of “year”"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1620
msgid "Two numbers decide the invoice"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:43
msgid "Two systems, one physical world"
msgstr "Dois sistemas, um mundo físico"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:734
msgid "Typical covalent bond lengths fall around one to two ångströms. X-ray crystallography papers often report lattice parameters in ångströms. Converting to nanometres is a shift by ×0.1: 1.54 Å = 0.154 nm. Converting to picometres multiplies by 100: 1.54 Å = 154 pm—sometimes preferred in quantum-chemistry outputs."
msgstr "Os comprimentos típicos das ligações covalentes ficam em torno de um a dois ångströms. Artigos de cristalografia de raios X frequentemente relatam parâmetros de rede em ångströms. A conversão para nanômetros é uma mudança de × 0,1: 1,54 Å = 0,154 nm. A conversão para picômetros multiplica por 100: 1,54 Å = 154 pm – às vezes preferido em resultados de química quântica."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:211
msgid "UI converters often hide the issue by rounding to a fixed number of decimals. Users see clean results and never notice the internal noise. Problems appear when another system consumes the raw float: a CAD kernel, a CSV export, or a unit test comparing strings of full precision."
msgstr "Os conversores de UI geralmente ocultam o problema arredondando para um número fixo de casas decimais. Os usuários veem resultados limpos e nunca percebem o ruído interno. Os problemas aparecem quando outro sistema consome o float bruto: um kernel CAD, uma exportação CSV ou um teste de unidade comparando strings de precisão total."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1328
msgid "Underlayment, adhesive, and trim are sometimes sold by length even when flooring is sold by area. Track quantity types separately so you do not treat a linear metre like a square metre."
msgstr "A base, o adesivo e o acabamento às vezes são vendidos por comprimento, mesmo quando o piso é vendido por área. Rastreie os tipos de quantidade separadamente para não tratar um metro linear como um metro quadrado."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2515
msgid "Understand L/100 km vs mpg thinking through speed, distance, and volume—convert trip length and pace correctly before you compare car efficiency figures."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1761
msgid "Understand the knot as a speed unit tied to the nautical mile, convert knots to km/h and mph, and avoid mixing statute miles with nautical miles in navigation."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:185
msgid "Understand why binary floating-point creates weird conversion residuals, when those errors matter, and how decimal or rational arithmetic keeps unit converters trustworthy."
msgstr "Entenda por que o ponto flutuante binário cria resíduos de conversão estranhos, quando esses erros são importantes e como a aritmética decimal ou racional mantém os conversores de unidades confiáveis."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1044
msgid "Unequal tolerances and fits (H7/g6 style thinking, even when expressed in inches historically) need special care. Convert the limiting sizes that define the fit, not just a single mid value."
msgstr "Tolerâncias e ajustes desiguais (pensamento estilo H7/g6, mesmo quando historicamente expressos em polegadas) precisam de cuidados especiais. Converta os tamanhos limites que definem o ajuste, não apenas um único valor médio."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1729
msgid "Unit conversion does not change stopping distance physics, but mixed mental models do. If you are used to thinking “60 mph needs X metres to stop,” rebuild that intuition in km/h before mountain descents abroad."
msgstr ""

